# AI call cost efficiency — always the cheapest correct call

Input tokens dominate this platform's LLM bill (~95% of a missed-opportunities
run). A prompt that re-sends the same large instruction block on every call is
the single biggest waste. When you add or change any LLM call, make it efficient
by default — but **never** by cutting evidence, coverage, or quality controls
(that trade is forbidden by [runtime-configuration](mdc:.cursor/rules/runtime-configuration.mdc)
and the cost brief in `docs/cursor_missed_opportunities_cost_efficiency.md`).

## Non-negotiables

- **Cache the stable prefix.** If a large system prompt (persona, rules, KB
  grounding, fixed instructions) is reused across many calls in a run, pass
  `cacheSystem: true` to `callChatModel`. Keep the `system` block byte-identical
  across calls and put everything per-call (transcript, IDs, timestamps, CRM
  evidence) in `user` — otherwise the prefix won't match and nothing caches.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — constant prefix cached, per-call data after the boundary
await callChatModel(provider, { system: sharedSystemPrompt, user: perCallEvidence, cacheSystem: true });

// ❌ BAD — per-call data folded into system defeats the cache and re-bills the prefix
await callChatModel(provider, { system: `${sharedSystemPrompt}\nCALL: ${conversationId}`, user });
```

- **Account for cache tokens in cost.** Anthropic reports cache write/read
  separately; price them via `estimateUsdCost(model, uncachedIn, out, cacheRead,
  cacheWrite)`. Thread `cacheReadTokens`/`cacheWriteTokens` from the result into
  `withCallLog`'s `CallLogResult`. Never charge cached reads at the full input
  rate. `tokens_in` stays TOTAL input (no DB column change).
- **Right-size the model and output.** Use the cheap tier unless the task needs
  the reasoning model; set `maxTokens` to the real output ceiling. Don't add a
  second model pass unless measured end-to-end savings justify it.
- **Don't re-send or duplicate context.** Do identity/date/dedupe/label work in
  code, not by asking the model. Reuse valid unchanged results instead of paying
  for identical inference again.

## Verify, don't assume

Confirm real cache hits from the provider usage fields (`cache_read_input_tokens`),
not from the request flag. A cost cut is only acceptable with the same evidence
coverage and no quality regression — measure both before claiming the saving.
